[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      143[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `tests/common/mod.rs` snapshots the *complete* observable state of a map after
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      144[0m:[38;5;10m[49m every single operation and diffs the C against the Rust:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      145[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      146[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * array header: `length`, `capacity`, `temp`, `hash_table` non-nullness;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      147[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * hash index: `slot_count`, `used_count`, `used_count_threshold`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      148[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `used_count_shrink_threshold`, `tombstone_count`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      149[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `tombstone_count_threshold`, `seed`, `slot_count_log2`, and the arena
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      150[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`remaining`, `block`, `mode`, storage non-nullness);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      151[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **every slot of every bucket**: all `slot_count` hash values and all
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      152[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `slot_count` indices, so probe order, tombstone placement and rehash layout
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      153[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   are compared bit-for-bit, not just the externally visible answers;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      154[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * the element payload — raw bytes for binary keys, the pointed-to strings plus
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      155[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the trailing value bytes for the pointer-key modes;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      156[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * the returned `*temp` / `header->temp` sentinel of every lookup and delete.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      157[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      158[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `table->temp_key` is deliberately excluded from the general snapshot because
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      159[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `stbds_make_hash_index` leaves it uninitialised; it is compared separately (by
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      160[0m:[38;5;10m[49m pointed-to string) right after each string-mode `hmput_key`, where the C does
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      161[0m:[38;5;10m[49m define it.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      162[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      163[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Raw pointer *values* are never compared (the two libraries have independent
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      164[0m:[38;5;10m[49m allocators), except where the C's contract is pointer identity — the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      165[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `arrgrowf` no-op path and the `hmput_default` no-op path, which assert
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      166[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `returned == input` on both sides.
